{"assertions":[{"answerability":"answerable","basis":"Breen's article \"Acts of the Apostles\" in the Catholic Encyclopedia (vol. 1, 1907): \"Writers are quite concordant in placing the date of Paul's coming to Rome in the year 62; hence the year 64 is the most probable date for the Acts.\" The article says of itself that \"we may at most assign a probable date for the completion of the book\".","basis_class":"traditional-catholic","date":"about 64 A.D.","derived":false,"disposition":"preferred","inherited":true,"label":"the year 64 is the most probable date","note":"The figure is the article's own inference from Paul's arrival at Rome in 62 plus the two years of Acts xxviii, 30, not an independently attested date; the same encyclopedia's St. Paul article instead puts the departure for Rome in 59 and the Roman captivity at 60-62, which would move it. Jerome (De viris illustribus 7) ties the book's composition to Rome and to the terminus of its narrative in \"the fourth year of Nero\", giving no A.D. year; that regnal reckoning is not converted here.","precision":"approximate-year","profile":"catholic-traditional-v1","relation":"composition","reporting_exception":null,"scope":"Acts","sources":["artifact.catholic-encyclopedia.volume-1.new-york-1907.newadvent-01117a-582c8526"],"subject":"composition.acts-of-the-apostles","title":"The Acts of the Apostles"},{"answerability":"answerable","basis":"The Catholic Encyclopedia's \"St. Paul\" (Prat, vol. 11) chronological table prints \"second mission, 50-53\".","basis_class":"traditional-catholic","date":"50 A.D.-53 A.D.","derived":false,"disposition":"disputed","inherited":true,"label":"second mission, 50-53","note":"","precision":"range","profile":"catholic-traditional-v1","relation":"narrated-event","reporting_exception":null,"scope":"Acts.15.36- Acts.16 Acts.17 Acts.18.1-22","sources":["artifact.catholic-encyclopedia.volume-11.new-york-1911.newadvent-11567b-bff0dda8"],"subject":"apostolic-age.saint-paul-second-mission","title":"St Paul's Second Missionary Journey"},{"answerability":"answerable","basis":"The Catholic Encyclopedia's \"Biblical Chronology\" (Howlett, vol. 3) gives a different span: the second journey \"ended not very long before the third missionary expedition began, probably in 54, and began about three years previously, in 51.\"","basis_class":"traditional-catholic","date":"51 A.D.-54 A.D.","derived":false,"disposition":"disputed","inherited":true,"label":"began about three years previously, in 51 ... probably in 54","note":"Hedged throughout (\"probably\", \"about three years previously\"), and tied to this article's council date of 51.","precision":"range","profile":"catholic-traditional-v1","relation":"narrated-event","reporting_exception":null,"scope":"Acts.15.36- Acts.16 Acts.17 Acts.18.1-22","sources":["artifact.catholic-encyclopedia.volume-3.new-york-1908.newadvent-03731a-f5f96f04"],"subject":"apostolic-age.saint-paul-second-mission","title":"St Paul's Second Missionary Journey"}],"chronology_status":"dated","locus":"Acts.16.14","reason":"","requested_profile":"catholic-comprehensive-v1","resolved_profiles":{"composition":"catholic-traditional-v1","narrated-event":"catholic-traditional-v1"},"status":"ok","v":1}
